--TEST--
a call to an extension's class needs the capabilities its manifest requests on the calling namespace's `[grants]` line, and an extension that requests nothing needs none — `rule:security/extension-grants-are-an-intersection`
--EXTENSION--
courier
ledger
--FILE--
<?nvs
// This file is the application. It may call every extension.
autoload 'Acme\Maps' from './maps';

echo Shop\Courier::version(), "\n";
echo Acme\Maps\Client::version(), "\n";
echo Acme\Maps\Client::echo(7), "\n";
--FILE maps/Client.nvs--
<?nvs
// The line for `Acme\Maps` is empty.
namespace Acme\Maps;

final class Client
{
    // `Shop\Courier` requests files and a host, so this call needs `fs.read` and `net.connect`.
    public static function version(): int
    {
        return Shop\Courier::version();
    }

    // `Shop\Ledger` requests nothing, so this call needs no capability.
    public static function echo(int $value): int
    {
        return Shop\Ledger::echoInt($value);
    }
}
--FILE package.toml--
# covers: tools:config/extension-grants-what-a-component-may-reach
[grants]
'Acme\Maps' = []
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0658]: the namespace `Acme\Maps` does not have the capability `fs.read`, `net.connect`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
